<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan BSPA buys 54,000 tonnes soybeans at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan BSPA buys 54,000 tonnes soybeans at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Taichung division of Taiwan's Breakfast Soybean Procurement Association bought a 54,000-tonne shipment of Brazilian or Argentine soybeans from Andre at a tender on Wednesday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The tender specifies that the soybeans could be sourced either in Brazil or Argentina, traders said.</p>
<p>The breakfast association's Taichung division comprises Sino Japan Feed Corp, Chia Hsin, Formosa Oilseed, Fwu Sow Grain and Tay Shan.  </p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p> Type		    Tonnes  Date/Location   Prices/Futures</p>
<p>				     Argentine/</p>
<p>				     Brazil port</p>
<p>Argentine/Brazilian 54,000  July 26-Aug 14  150 US cents/Sep</p>
<p>-- George Hsu, Taipei newsroom (886-2-5080815)</p>
